{
  "_comment": [
    "Synthetic tenant used by the export tests. Shaped deliberately:",
    "  - 1, 2 and 3 each have TWO children of the same type. A parent with only",
    "    one child cannot expose a loop that processes only the first child.",
    "  - 5 -> 2 closes a cycle (1 -> 2 -> 5 -> 2).",
    "  - 4 is a child of both 2 and 3, so it must still be exported only once.",
    "  - 8 and 9 are reachable only through an addition, so the default",
    "    --childTypes must not reach them.",
    "  - 8 has no name; others carry quotes, #, [, a tab and non-ASCII.",
    "  - 1, 2 and 4 carry external identities; 2 carries TWO, because the",
    "    identity loop can be truncated the same way the child loop can.",
    "    4's external id contains a space.",
    "  - 2 carries measurements, events and alarms, several of each, so a",
    "    truncated batch or loop is visible. Its event e2 has an attachment",
    "    (c8y_IsBinary) and its alarms are one CLEARED then one ACTIVE, which",
    "    is the order import has to preserve for alarm de-duplication.",
    "  - 4 carries measurements only, to prove per-type selection.",
    "  - alarm a3's text holds escaped JSON with quotes and newlines, which",
    "    must survive the round trip without its backslashes being doubled.",
    "    Keep it."
  ],
